  "question": {
    "text": "The correct option(s) to distinguish nitrate salts of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> taken separately is (are)<br />\r<br />\r(1) <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> shows the characteristic green colour in the flame test<br />\r<br />\r(2) only <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> shows the formation of precipitate by passing <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> in acidic medium<br />\r<br />\r(3) only <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> shows the formation of precipitate by passing <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> in faintly basic medium<br />\r<br />\r(4) <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>Cu</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow> </msup> <mo>|</mo><mtext>Cu</mtext></mrow> </math> has higher reduction potential than <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>Mn</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow> </msup> <mo>|</mo><mtext>Mn</mtext></mrow> </math> (measured under similar conditions)"
